1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
This is HireXpert: expert work, without the hiring wait.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The median role takes 39 days to fill, says SHRM. A business starts here, once.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Harbor Dental types its name and drops in a denial letter. One click, and we start building its private digital workspace.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:31,670
Ready in about four minutes, measured live.

5
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:39,330
This is its own Superserve machine: VS Code in the browser, its documents, and three specialist AI agents installed.

6
00:00:39,330 --> 00:00:47,000
Now it posts a job: appeal a denied MRI claim.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Maya has good judgment but no credential. She claims the job from the board, requests access, and is let into that same workspace.

8
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:19,000
She drafts the appeal letter right beside the documents, then submits it for verification.

9
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Three agents, running on OpenAI Codex, talk over Agent Relay. Policy, billing codes, appeals.

10
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
They check every line against the documents, cite sources, and reply verified or fix needed.

11
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Here they caught two fixes, all three voted, and Maya accepts the fixes before anything goes out.

12
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:43,000
The business reviews and pays. Terse holds the whole case: documents, deadlines, votes. It wakes itself on deadlines and escalates to a supervisor.

13
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Nothing is lost on restart. A certified biller is about $25 an hour, says BLS. Here, it's $15.

14
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
HireXpert. Hire the judgment, not the credential.

